==English==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|politesse|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it}} {{term|politezza||lang=it}}, from {{term|polito||lang=it}}, past participle of {{term|pulire||lang=it|to polish, clean}} from {{etyl|la}} {{term|polire||lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/pɒlɪˈtɛs/}}
*{{a|US}} {{IPA|/pɑləˈtɛs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# [[civility|Civility]], [[politeness]], [[courtesy]] or [[gallantry]]; or an instance of this.
#*'''1978''', Iris Murdoch, ''The Sea, The Sea'', Vintage 1999, pp. 56-7:
#*:The reference in his letter to ‘having a drink’ is of course just an empty '''''politesse'''''.

